        <h2>
          The fix is the<br>
 easy half.
        </h2>
      

      
        <div class="lvg-truth-scorecard__two">

          
            <div>
              <p>Most products in this category are sold on the fix. Clear the breakout, fade the mark, get through the week. That is worth something, and LNGVTY does it too.</p><p>The other half is whether it comes back. If the visible concern was the endpoint of something underneath — and the previous part of this story argues that it was — then clearing it without improving anything underneath leaves the exact conditions that produced it still in place.</p>
            </div>
          

          
            <div>
              <p>So it returns, and you buy the fix again. That is the loop from part one, running inside a single product.</p><p>A multi-repair serum works on the concern and on the conditions at the same time. As the skin functions better, today's problem resolves — and the likelihood of it recurring falls, because resilience was being built the whole way through.</p>
            </div>
          

        </div>
      

